    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Heat the oil in a wide pot over medium heat. Add the pork and cook, stirring now and then, until it renders some fat and turns lightly golden.",
        "minutes": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the garlic and onion and cook until soft, then add the tomatoes and cook until they soften.",
        "minutes": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Stir in the bagoong alamang and cook for a minute so it loses its raw smell.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Pour in the water and add the squash. Cover and simmer until the squash is half cooked.",
        "minutes": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the sitaw, okra and ampalaya. Cover and simmer.",
        "minutes": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the eggplant, cover and cook until all the vegetables are tender.",
        "minutes": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Press a few cubes of squash against the side of the pot to thicken the sauce. Season with pepper, taste for salt and serve with rice.",
        "minutes": null
      }
    ],
    "tips": "Brands of bagoong alamang vary a lot in saltiness. Start with 2 tablespoons and add the rest at the end if the sauce needs it."
